 "id": "s3h",
 "title": "Supply joins by hand: U301, U501 pin 18, the VBAT_PROT sense node at U201 and U202",
 "why": "U301: the regulator's output ran round its east side and walled VBAT_PROT pins 1 and 2 off from C301. It now runs from pin 6 down the chip's west side to C302 (0.15 mm, 2.6 mm long: a via nearer would stand in the T1S trunk's corridor or on the RMII line under it), and from C302's via on F.Cu to R301. U501 pin 18 (3V3) gets a 0.35/0.20 mm via in its pad. U201 pins 15/16 and U202 pin 8 (VBAT_PROT sense) join on B.Cu and share one via into the VBAT_PROT strip of In2 and In3 (y 71 to 73) at (161.41, 71.7): under them the inner layers are VBAT_D, and VBAT_PROT may not run on F.Cu under the GND bar. HGATE's via moves into U201 pin 14's pad to let pins 15/16 out. Three stray vias of round s1 go.",
